@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain

-- g8-fees-nouns.l4: the nouns of group G8 (the Fees Regulations in three vintages and the SimpLEX test table).
-- DECLARE only: no rule and no #EVAL.  Every other g8- module imports this one.
-- Written by the G8 encoder.  The shared nouns of the fleet are in domain.l4, which is read-only; the nouns
-- below are the ones that only the Fees Regulations need.  Where a noun here duplicates what a later
-- INTEGRATOR step might move into domain.l4, FRAGMENT-G8.md lists it under "nouns requests".
--
-- The test for membership is the fleet's: could a witness of ordinary competence testify to the fact?
-- Which vintage a rule belongs to, which service a person asked for, how much they paid, and what a
-- gazette printed are facts; what the regulations make of them is a rule and lives in the other modules.

§ `Vintages and services`

@ref Fees Regulations as made (KT 11951), as amended (KT 12383), SimpLEX draft (Figure 4)
@desc The three texts of the Fees Regulations the fleet holds, each a separate answer; a lookup takes one of them as an input and never borrows a figure from another
DECLARE `Vintage of the Fees Regulations` IS ONE OF
    `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations`   -- Figure 4 of Schwartz, Bar-Siman-Tov and Gelbard (2025), screenshot only: regs 1 and 2 are visible, regs 3 to 5 are not
    `the Fees Regulations as made`                -- Kovetz HaTakanot 11951, 9.7.2025
    `the Fees Regulations as amended`             -- Kovetz HaTakanot 12383, 4.5.2026, over the text as made

@ref Law s.59
@desc Everything a person can be charged for under section 59 of the Law, including the heads that no vintage prices, so that silence about a head is an answer a lookup can give
DECLARE `Service under the Fees Regulations` IS ONE OF
    `the service of filing an application for a licence or its renewal`                                  -- s.59 head: "submitting a licence application" (priced only by the draft, reg.2(d))
    `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal`                                                  -- s.59 head: "granting a licence or renewing it" (priced by reg.2(c) as made)
    `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal`       -- s.59, second limb (priced by reg.2(e) of the draft and 2(d) as made)
    `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence`                                  -- s.59, second limb: "the grant of a temporary licence" (priced by no vintage)
    `the service of sitting a practical exam`                                                            -- s.59 head: "exams required to receive a final certificate"
    `the service of sitting a theoretical exam`                                                          -- the same head
    `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam`                                          -- s.59 head: "including an objection to exams"
    `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam`                                        -- the same head
    `the service of attending a continuing training course`                                              -- s.59 head: "training courses under section 17" (priced by no vintage)

@ref Fees Regulations, regulation 1, definitions of practical exam and theoretical exam
@desc An exam taken in a vocational training course, as the facts a witness can state about its content and its examinee; whether it is a "practical exam" or a "theoretical exam" is regulation 1's rule
DECLARE `Exam in a vocational training course` HAS
    `assesses the practical knowledge and skills of the learner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `assesses the knowledge and deep understanding of the learner in theoretical subjects` IS A BOOLEAN
    `taken by a learner in a vocational training course` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on subjects in the curriculum for the installation and service of cooling facilities` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(a) to (d)
@desc The persons the regulations name as paying; the draft's regulation 2 names none
DECLARE `Payer under the Fees Regulations` IS ONE OF
    `the examinee under the Fees Regulations`            -- reg.2(a) and (a1): "the examinee"
    `the objector under the Fees Regulations`            -- reg.2(b): "the person who lodges the objection"
    `the licence applicant under the Fees Regulations`   -- reg.2(c) and (d): "the applicant for the licence"

@ref Fees Regulations, regulation 2
@desc What one vintage prints for one service: the figure as printed, the provision that prints it in that vintage's own numbering, who pays, and the day the printed figure took effect
DECLARE `Fee stated in a vintage` HAS
    `the amount stated` IS A NUMBER @desc The figure as the text prints it, in new shekels, before any update under regulation 3
    `the provision that states it` IS A STRING @desc The sub-regulation in the vintage's own numbering, for example 2(a1)
    `the payer the provision names` IS A MAYBE `Payer under the Fees Regulations` @desc NOTHING where the vintage names nobody
    `the day the stated amount took effect` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day from which the printed figure applied; NOTHING for the draft, which never took effect
    `an objection charge rather than a fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True for the objection charge (the text says "an amount", not "a fee"); regulation 3(a) updates "the amounts of the fees" in regulation 2, and whether it reaches this amount is a fork

§ `Regulation 3: what a reading of the update can vary`

-- The forks of regulation 3 are carried as one record, so that each alternative is a value that can be handed
-- to the same function.  The values the encoding takes are in g8-fees-as-made.l4 as `the reading the encoding takes`.

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a)
@desc How an exact half shekel is rounded; regulation 3(a) says only "to the nearest whole new shekel"
DECLARE `Rounding of a half shekel` IS ONE OF
    `a half shekel is rounded up`
    `a half shekel is rounded to the even shekel`
    `a half shekel is rounded down`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a)
@desc When the rounding is done: after every update day, or once after the last
DECLARE `When regulation 3 rounds` IS ONE OF
    `regulation 3 rounds after every update day`
    `regulation 3 rounds once, after the last update day`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a)
@desc Which index the base index is for the first update day: "the index published in the month before the commencement"
DECLARE `Base index of the first update day` IS ONE OF
    `the index published in the month before the commencement`
    `the index relating to the month before the commencement`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a)
@desc From which update day an amount that took effect after the regulations commenced is updated
DECLARE `First update of an amount fixed later` IS ONE OF
    `the first 1 January after the amount took effect`
    `the first 1 January after the regulations commenced`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(b) and regulation 3(a)
@desc Whether regulation 3(a), which updates "the amounts of the fees" in regulation 2, reaches the objection charge, which regulation 2(b) calls "an amount" and not "a fee"
DECLARE `Whether regulation 3 updates the objection charge` IS ONE OF
    `regulation 3 updates the objection charge as a fee`
    `regulation 3 leaves the objection charge as printed`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a) and (b)
@desc From when an update binds: its update day, or the day the Director General's notice under regulation 3(b) was published
DECLARE `Day an update binds from` IS ONE OF
    `an update binds from its update day`
    `an update binds from the day of the Director General's notice`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(b)
@desc One notice of the Director General of the Ministry of Labour under regulation 3(b)
DECLARE `Fee update notice` HAS
    `year of the update day` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the 1 January whose update the notice announces
    `published in Reshumot on` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice was published

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3
@desc The forks of regulation 3 as one value; the encoding takes one value of it and the tests hand the others to the same functions
DECLARE `Reading of regulation 3` HAS
    `a half shekel` IS A `Rounding of a half shekel`
    `the rounding` IS A `When regulation 3 rounds`
    `the base index` IS A `Base index of the first update day`
    `a later amount` IS A `First update of an amount fixed later`
    `an update` IS A `Day an update binds from`
    `the objection charge` IS A `Whether regulation 3 updates the objection charge`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3
@desc Everything regulation 3 reads besides the stated amount: the index readings, the day the regulations commenced, one reading of the forks, and the Director General's notices
DECLARE `Inputs of regulation 3` HAS
    `index readings` IS A LIST OF `Price index reading` @desc Every reading of the consumer price index the caller holds; the sources give none
    `the regulations came into force on` IS A DATE @desc The commencement day of the Fees Regulations as made; regulation 3(a) keys its first update day and its first base index on it
    `the reading of regulation 3` IS A `Reading of regulation 3` @desc The values the forks of regulation 3 take
    `notices of the Director General` IS A LIST OF `Fee update notice` @desc Every notice under regulation 3(b) the caller holds; used only by the reading that makes an update bind from its notice

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a) "the month before their commencement"
@desc A calendar month, as a year and a month number; month arithmetic on these numbers never touches a date
DECLARE `Calendar month under regulation 3` HAS
    `year of the calendar month` IS A NUMBER
    `number of the calendar month` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 to 12

§ `Regulations 2 to 4: the other forks`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4
@desc What regulation 4 asks about a service: whether a fee was fixed for it under the regulations, and whether the person who must pay it paid it in full
DECLARE `Facts regulation 4 asks about` HAS
    `a fee was fixed under the regulations for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the vintage prices the service
    `the payer paid the fee in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the payer paid the whole of the fee the vintage fixes

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(b)
@desc What "in addition to the payment of the fee as stated in sub-regulation (a)" asks of the person who objects
DECLARE `Reading of the objection charge` IS ONE OF
    `the objection charge alone`                                      -- NIS 40 per objection and nothing else
    `the fee of the exam objected to and the objection charge`        -- the exam's own fee, then NIS 40 per objection
    `the fee that the cross-referenced sub-regulation states and the objection charge`  -- literally the fee of the sub-regulation the text names

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(b)
@desc Whether the regulation 2(b) of the text as made, which speaks of "the exam", reaches an objection to the score of a theoretical exam
DECLARE `Reading of "the exam" in regulation 2(b) as made` IS ONE OF
    `the exam is the one exam the regulations define`   -- the practical exam only
    `the exam is any exam`                              -- practical and theoretical

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4
@desc What regulation 4 does where a vintage fixes no fee for the service it is asked about
DECLARE `Reading of regulation 4 where no fee is fixed` IS ONE OF
    `regulation 4 is not engaged`      -- the bar speaks of a service "for which a fee was fixed"; none was, so nothing bars it
    `regulation 4 refuses to say`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4
@desc Whether regulation 4's bar on giving a licence reaches a temporary licence whose fee is fixed for its application
DECLARE `Reading of regulation 4 and a temporary licence` IS ONE OF
    `the fee fixed for the application binds the grant of the temporary licence`
    `only a fee fixed for the licence itself binds its grant`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4
@desc Whether a payer who paid nothing has not paid "in full" a fee that is fixed at a positive figure without the updated figure of regulation 3 being known
DECLARE `Reading of regulation 4 where nothing was paid` IS ONE OF
    `a payer who paid nothing has not paid in full, whatever the update`
    `the updated figure decides even where nothing was paid`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4
@desc Whether a payment above the fee is a payment of the fee "in full"
DECLARE `Reading of payment in full` IS ONE OF
    `a payment of at least the fee is payment in full`
    `only a payment of exactly the fee is payment in full`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4
@desc The forks of regulation 4 as one value; the encoding takes one value of it and the tests hand the others to the same functions
DECLARE `Reading of regulation 4` HAS
    `a service with no fee` IS A `Reading of regulation 4 where no fee is fixed`
    `a temporary licence` IS A `Reading of regulation 4 and a temporary licence`
    `payment in full` IS A `Reading of payment in full`
    `nothing was paid` IS A `Reading of regulation 4 where nothing was paid`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(b) and regulation 4
@desc The acts that regulation 3(b) and regulation 4 are about, as acts and not as section names
DECLARE `Act under the Fees Regulations` IS ONE OF
    `give a licence for which a fee was fixed`
    `renew a licence for which a fee was fixed`
    `allow the performance of an exam for which a fee was fixed`
    `allow the lodging of an objection for which a fee was fixed`
    `publish in Reshumot the text of regulation 2 as changed by the update`
